# MC-X-F12 (writer 9): rate's rows govern always, but a row reads base, whose row governs 2027..: inputs and
# bands "are read at the law date of their reader" (L §4.3), so rate's value can change with the law date (L
# §4.3: law-dated), and r reads it with no at (P-6: the chain of readers of base goes on through rate).
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source act "the act"

input age3: int
input base: money PLN
band rate(a: int): money PLN
def r[m in months]: money PLN = rate(age3)
ask q: r[2027-05]

version v_law
  cite act
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  base = 400.00 PLN "the base"

version v_act
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-12-01
  age3 = 3 "the age"
  rate: [0, 6) = base "under 6"
  rate: [6, 18) = 250.00 PLN "6 to 17"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE r reads law-dated facts and states no at (m.tally:13)
